ixed): (1) CANONICAL MASS-FORMULA SHAPE. The block writes 'The topological mass formula m(K) = Vol(K)/hbar_q^2'. The canonical shape per AGENTS.md is m(K) = m_e . Vol(K) . rho(K) / hbar_q^2 - both the electron scale m_e (CAL-1) and the per-block density rho(K) are missing here. The divergence conclusion is unaffected (rho and m_e are hbar_q-independent), but the formula as printed is the purged short form. (2) UNSUPPORTED PHYSICS CLAIM: 'consistent with the classical expectation that only unknotted particles have finite mass' - no such classical expectation exists in the literature; this reads as a post-hoc rationalisation of the divergence. Proposed: delete the clause or cite what asserts it. (3) VERIFIED CORRECT: J_K(1) = 1 for every KNOT (the block correctly says knot - for an L-component link the value is (-2)^{L-1}); at q = 1 the Hecke quadratic has roots +-1 and H_n(R,q) -> k[S_n]; hbar_q = 1 - q^{-1} -> 0 and c_q = 1/(q-1) -> infinity; V^{(x)n} = (+) V_lambda (x) S_lambda keeps floor(n/2)+1 summands, consistent with the sibling proposition.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r07","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r07","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"warn","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/p